\section*{Near-critical Voronoi universality conditional on Cardy limits}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. Assuming critical Voronoi Cardy crossings, the authors claim a quenched universal joint limit of near-critical polygon-crossing thresholds, normalized by expected pivotal counts.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
At fixed typical tessellations, color-only exploration and arm estimates turn scalar crossing limits into joint SLE and loop information. Finite witnesses recover constrained polygon crossings, after which normalized pivotal dynamics identify the monotone near-critical threshold law in probability over geometries.

